From: JamesDSP root fork - 0005
Subject: [PATCH 0005] engine: honour EFFECT_BUFFER_ACCESS_ACCUMULATE on the
 process output buffer

Root cause of the "session-level JamesDSP chain mutes the output" family on
ROMs whose AudioFlinger gives session effects a real output buffer mapping
(measured on MTK HyperOS / Android 15, xaga):

AudioFlinger configures an effect with EFFECT_BUFFER_ACCESS_ACCUMULATE
whenever its input and output buffers differ (EffectModule::
requiredEffectBufferAccessMode).  For a per-session chain the output buffer
maps the output thread's shared mix, which already carries the contribution
of every other track and chain of that thread.  The contract is therefore
"ADD your rendered output to the out buffer"; all process paths of this
engine stored over it instead.  Consequences on xaga (all reproduced and
instrumented):

  - one enabled JamesDSP instance mounted on ANY session whose track
    delivers pure digital silence replaced the shared mix with silence:
    the whole output thread went mute ("threadLoop_write write muted data
    to hw") and stayed mute while the chain existed;
  - with several mounted instances only the last processed chain's audio
    survived (the earlier chains' contributions were overwritten);
  - single-session playback kept working because the chain input and
    output buffers alias there (ACCESS_WRITE, in-place transform).

Vendor insert effects mounted the same way (MiSound) accumulate and are
unaffected, which is what kept system effects working on the same ROM.

The fix renders into a private per-engine scratch buffer and adds the
result to the out buffer (saturating for int16/int32/int8_24), keeping the
historical replace behaviour for aliased buffers (ACCESS_WRITE), for
packed 24 bit, and when the scratch cannot be provided.  The engine-swap
crossfade path stops rendering into the shared buffer as well: it
crossfades the two engines' private outputs and adds the result.

Host tests: test_accum.c covers the accumulator modes and fallbacks;
native/test/run_tests.sh stays green.
